# daybook:managed start
# What is kept and what is thrown away. Three categories; only the middle one is listed in this file.
#   STATE    irreplaceable. Committed, always. If losing it costs something you cannot buy back, it is state.
#   CACHE    regenerable from a feed, a model or a build. Ignored, each line with its reason.
#   SECRETS  tokens and private URLs. Never committed. Restore re-authorises; see ~/Daybook/Index/RESTORE.md.
# Never list what to keep. List what is thrown away, and say why. Stamped from ~/Daybook/Index/templates/gitignore.

# CACHE — the OS and the tools leave these behind
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc
node_modules/
.venv/
*.tmp
# CACHE — the project page and its thumbnail, generated by the index from this project's own files
data/status/index.html
data/status/hero-thumb.jpg

# SECRETS — the names every project in Daybook uses for them
*token*.json
*secret*
*.pem
.env
# daybook:managed end

# CACHE — this project's own regenerable files, one line each with the reason
